{"Title":"An Act to preserve historic markers","BillNumber":"H3425","DocketNumber":"HD1491","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"PrimarySponsor":{"Id":"TMS2","Name":"Todd M. Smola","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/TMS2","ResponseDate":"2023-01-12T16:28:36.403"},"Cosponsors":[{"Id":"TMS2","Name":"Todd M. Smola","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/TMS2","ResponseDate":"2023-01-12T16:28:36.4033333"},{"Id":"NJO1","Name":"Norman J. Orrall","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/NJO1","ResponseDate":"2023-07-11T14:36:51.8733333"}],"JointSponsor":null,"BillHistory":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Documents/H3425/DocumentHistoryActions","LegislationTypeName":"Bill","Pinslip":"By Representative Smola of Warren, a petition (accompanied by bill, House, No. 3425) of Todd M. Smola for legislation to appropriate a certain sum of money to the Highway Department for the repair and preservation of historic markers.  Transportation.","DocumentText":"\tSECTION 1. There shall be appropriated a specified amount of not more than $200,000 for the Massachusetts Highway Department to pick-up, repaint, repair and refurbish the black upright markers at historic places installed pursuant to chapter 10 of the resolves of 1930.\t\r\n","EmergencyPreamble":null,"RollCalls":[],"Attachments":[],"CommitteeRecommendations":[{"Action":"Favorable","FiscalAmounts":[],"Committee":{"CommitteeCode":"J27","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Committees/J27"},"Votes":[]}],"Amendments":[]}